{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/143052-inspired-inspiration","id":143052,"title":"Inspired Inspiration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-19T21:55:44-07:00","id":143052,"title":"Inspired Inspiration","content":"What Characters From old Fiction , Myth or Real Life would make an good Inspired?<br /> <br /> <br /> Captain Nemo - A baddass stalwart Captain with Mad Science<br /> Merlin- Not a Sorcerer but a Powerful Mesmerist<br /> Harry Houdini- the typical Daredevil<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T12:09:55-07:00","id":144674,"title":"","content":"Weeeell...<br /> Not the most original people for me to start with but here's some classic fictional characters:<br /> <br /> Indiana Jones - Resourceful Daredevil that constantly outsmart, outfight and outrun enemies of superior power and resources.<br /> <br /> Doc Savage - Can't think of anyone that's a more stereotypical Stalwart. A supergenius scientist and superpowered adventurer with an implacable moral code. Most likely one of the inspirations for the games Primoris<br /> <br /> Fu Manchu - A diabolical genius whose mesmerist powers can twist the mind of even the most resilient and turn the greatest of friends into the deadliest of foes.<br /> <br /> The Shadow - Unrelenting vigilante of justice. His mesmerist powers allow him to both &quot;know what evil lurks in the hearts of men&quot; as well as to &quot;cloud men's mind&quot; to move and strike unseen.<br /> <br /> Rick Blaine - Smooth, calm and collected. His current career as a simple nightclub owner in Casablanca hides a colorful past. Though a mere mortal, this Daredevil shows the full capabilities of humans: No woman can resist him and no man can stand against him. That is, whenever he can get his head out of the bottle.<br /> <br /> And a real life daredevil as well:<br /> <br /> Amelia Earhart - Fearless and talented, this woman would not let social mores or silly gender expectations choke out her adventurous spirit . Lost to the world, we must wonder: Did tragedy befall her? Or did her journey lead her to discover wonders and fortunes beyond the imagination of us lesser mortals?<br /> And now with her gone what will become of her legacy, The Ninety-Nines? What adventures await this organization of all-female pilots in the times to come?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2030-baboonking","name":"baboonking","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2030_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T12:17:10-07:00","id":144699,"title":"","content":"Actually, I think most roles played by Humphrey Bogart might fit well as Daredevils.<br /> ...So I'm just gonna skip ahead and declare Bogart a Daredevil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2030-baboonking","name":"baboonking","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2030_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T12:51:47-07:00","id":144747,"title":"","content":"From real life:<br /> Nicola Tesla, hyper-intelligent Stalwart.<br /> Teddy Roosevelt, tough as nails Daredevil.<br /> Audie L Murphy, I think he's some kind of rare combo of a Daredevil AND a Stalwart.....might even be an early Nova.....dude was crazy skilled and lucky and tough. First entry on Wikipedia for him mentions how he got his Medal of Honor. He fought off a company of Germans, by himself, at age 19, then went on to lead a counter-offensive while wounded and out of ammo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T13:15:41-07:00","id":144779,"title":"","content":"Possible real-life examples:<br /> <br /> Daniel M'Mburugu (Fists of Stone, Lightning Reflexes)<br /> Craig Harrison (Eagle Eyes, Trick Shot)<br /> Chesley Sullenberger (Perfect Poise, Wheelman/Barnstormer, and a good use of Dramatic Editing)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T20:51:03-07:00","id":145242,"title":"","content":"Howard Hughes - Industrialist, aviator, filmmaker, philantropist! What kind of inspired would he be? I'm leaning towards Stalwart","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2030-baboonking","name":"baboonking","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2030_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T21:10:27-07:00","id":145260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>baboonking</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/143052-inspired-inspiration?p=145242#post145242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Howard Hughes - Industrialist, aviator, filmmaker, philantropist! What kind of inspired would he be? I'm leaning towards Stalwart</div> </div> </div> </div> He never really demonstrated superhuman talents -- he was just extraordinarily good and successful in his areas of focus. I'd suggest he'd be a Daredevil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T21:37:53-07:00","id":145271,"title":"","content":"Interestingly, in the pulps, the Shadow was a mere vigilante. A couple of stories have the villains seeing the Shadow's &quot;true face&quot; and remark that he is a man of many faces with no true face of his own. Sounds very much like a <b>stalwart</b> shape-changing ability. Interestingly enough, the Shadow is Kent Allard, with Lamont Cranston being a separate character whose identity Kent assumed from time to time.<br /> <br /> In the radio drama, they couldn't easily describe to viewers how and where the Shadow was hiding, so they introduced the idea of the Shadow having spent some time in the east and learning the ability to hypnotically cloud men's minds, making him almost certainly a <b>mesmerist</b>. For simplicity's sake, the Kent Allard identity was dropped and the Shadow was simply Cranston. This version, the millionaire vigilante detective cloaked in darkness, is almost certainly the origin of heroes like Batman.<br /> <br /> I believe one of the radio stories off-handedly mentions that the ability to become nearly invisible is &quot;a technology soon to be available to police officers everywhere,&quot; implying the super-science of a <b>daredevil</b>.<br /> <br /> So really, depending on which interpretation you prefer, the Shadow -- and many pulp characters -- could fit into any of the three Inspired types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T21:47:54-07:00","id":145276,"title":"","content":"Everyone's story is different -- which means there are as many wonderful stories to tell as there are Adventurers! to tell them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T21:53:20-07:00","id":145301,"title":"","content":"I wonder how many Maxwells there are... And how many Michaels? How many times did Annabelle's story end tragically, and are there any stories where she survived? Are there any stories where Thetis had second thoughts about her plans? Any times where Hope never died, selfishness was Sacrificed instead of humanity, and a bright new tomorrow was faced in Unity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2464,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","user":"lustral_star","date":". 05-22-2014, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T23:47:43-07:00","id":145349,"title":"","content":"some more Ideas<br /> <br /> <br /> Bob Morane - a Daredevil with Military experience . Together with his Friend Bill Ballantine ( a stalwart) he gets out of every dire Situation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Count Dracula- Vampires? yeaaahh suuure. The truth is that the count, is one of the most powerful stalwarts in History ( in fact already a Nova) he posesses knacks wich allows him to drain vital energys from other people to sustain himself. He also posesses a Hibernation knack ,with wich he is able to sleep through Centuries without ageing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tarzan- a stalwart with heighten Senses and agility, his Brainfuncionts are able to Interprete the Language of Animals<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T12:14:58-07:00","id":145903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/143052-inspired-inspiration?p=145271#post145271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestingly, in the pulps, the Shadow was a mere vigilante. A couple of stories have the villains seeing the Shadow's &quot;true face&quot; and remark that he is a man of many faces with no true face of his own. Sounds very much like a <b>stalwart</b> shape-changing ability. Interestingly enough, the Shadow is Kent Allard, with Lamont Cranston being a separate character whose identity Kent assumed from time to time.<br /> <br /> In the radio drama, they couldn't easily describe to viewers how and where the Shadow was hiding, so they introduced the idea of the Shadow having spent some time in the east and learning the ability to hypnotically cloud men's minds, making him almost certainly a <b>mesmerist</b>. For simplicity's sake, the Kent Allard identity was dropped and the Shadow was simply Cranston. This version, the millionaire vigilante detective cloaked in darkness, is almost certainly the origin of heroes like Batman.<br /> <br /> I believe one of the radio stories off-handedly mentions that the ability to become nearly invisible is &quot;a technology soon to be available to police officers everywhere,&quot; implying the super-science of a <b>daredevil</b>.<br /> <br /> So really, depending on which interpretation you prefer, the Shadow -- and many pulp characters -- could fit into any of the three Inspired types.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm most familiar with the radio serials so that's what I go with. You can find them fairly easy on the internet as there's a couple of websites out there dedicated to nostalgic radio shows that lets you listen to them for free. I knew the whole thing about the mystical &quot;cloud men's mind&quot; thing was an invention of the serial but I didn't know that one suggested that the invisibility thing was technological. That's pretty cool.<br /> Not too familiar with the books, though. If anyone got any ideas on where one might find some of these stories (either for free or for a reasonable price) feel free to share.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Ian. I'm really excited about the new Trinity Continuum games. The original Trinity was both the first RPG I ever played AND the first RPG I was the storyteller for. Nice to see that it is coming back along with Adventure! and Aberrant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2030,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2030-baboonking","user":"baboonking","date":". 05-22-2014, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2030-baboonking","name":"baboonking","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2030_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T12:28:24-07:00","id":145909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/143052-inspired-inspiration?p=145260#post145260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> He never really demonstrated superhuman talents -- he was just extraordinarily good and successful in his areas of focus. I'd suggest he'd be a Daredevil.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going back and forth between those two. The thing that made me (hesitantly) lean towards Stalwart was that he had so freaking many things that were his area of expertise that it seemed almost unreal.<br /> I just get an almost-too-good-to-be-true vibe from him which reminded me more of a Stalwart. But I agree that Daredevil could also be appropriate. I haven't read the Adventure! book in a while so I might be a bit fuzzy on what belong to each archetype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2030-baboonking","name":"baboonking","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2030_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T09:58:25-07:00","id":148751,"title":"","content":"In fiction:<br /> <br /> Erica Bain (The Brave One): Daredevil (Forgettable, Indomitable Will, Instant Expert, Trick Shot, Untouchable)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T15:02:16-07:00","id":153096,"title":"","content":"In fiction:<br /> <br /> Frank Martin (The Transporter): Daredevil (Enhanced Impact, Lightning Reflexes, Navigation Hazard, One Man Army, Wheelman)<br /> <br /> Real life:<br /> <br /> Colin Furze (Check out his YouTube channel): Daredevil (Gadgeteer)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T07:43:07-07:00","id":153826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/143052-inspired-inspiration?p=153096#post153096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Colin Furze (Check out his YouTube channel): Daredevil (Gadgeteer)</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Yes. Always and forever, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1006-widdershawns","name":"widdershawns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1006_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T09:21:52-07:00","id":153934,"title":"","content":"I realized he was probably a Gadgeteer when he made working Wolverine claws and walked on his ceiling with magnet shoes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T12:54:20-07:00","id":160160,"title":"","content":"Adam and Jamie<br /> <br /> Batman.<br /> <br /> Arsene Lupin<br /> <br /> Roland Deschain<br /> <br /> Tony Stark","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https: